course: dictionary
lesson: 13821
title: Isolated: far away, alone, or just once
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Isolated» means far away from other places, towns or people. It can describe a place, a person, an event or something kept apart. «The farm sat isolated at the end of a long dirt road, miles from the nearest town.» The clues are long dirt road and miles from the nearest town, so isolated means remote, with no other homes close by.
explain: The word can also describe a feeling. «Since moving to a new country, Amira felt isolated, because she had no friends at school yet.» Amira is not miles from anyone, so isolated here means lonely: she has little contact with others. Ask what the clues say about her, not just about the place.
explain: Sometimes «isolated» means happening only once. «The mistake was an isolated case, not a habit.» An isolated case is one that happens rarely, not as part of a pattern. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: if «only once» still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: «Isolated» means far away from other places, towns or people.
fact: «Isolated» can also mean feeling alone, as in «feel isolated».
fact: «An isolated incident» means something happened only once or rarely.
fact: «Isolated» can mean kept apart from others, for example to stop an illness spreading.
fact: Tristan da Cunha is a very remote island in the South Atlantic Ocean, so it is a good example of an isolated place.
exercise: «The isolated village had no road, only a track through the hills.» What does isolated mean here? | *Far away from other places | Very rich and busy | Painted bright blue | Full of friendly people
exercise: «Since she changed schools, Maya has felt isolated.» What does isolated suggest? | Full of energy and ready to run | Lost in a big shop | Sleepy after lunch | *Alone, with little contact with others
exercise: «The missed spelling was an isolated case, not a habit.» What does an isolated case mean? | A very large case | *A case that happens only once or rarely | A case that happens every day | A case about a box
test: «Sam was isolated in a separate room while he had the flu, so the germs would not spread.» What does isolated mean here? | Happy to play outside | *Kept apart from others | Lost in a crowd | Very famous
test: Ms Lee says, «The island is isolated.» Which clue would best help you check? | It is full of crowded streets | It has a big shopping centre | *It is many miles from the nearest land | It is the same as the town next door
exam: Jayden reads «She lives in an isolated farmhouse, but she is never lonely.» Which meaning fits best? | Kept apart from her family for a rule | *Far from other homes, so it describes the place | Happening only once | Happy to play with friends every day
